-- title:
--   Mod p Hecke eigensystems come from characters of T
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N\ge 1$ a natural number, $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ a set of naturals, and $k$ an integer with $2\le k$; let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$, let $\varphi\in F[\![X]\!]$ be a formal power series and let $\lambda,\mu\colon\mathbb{N}\to F$ be arbitrary functions. Assume: (i) $\varphi$ lies in `modPCusp N k F`, the $F$-span inside $F[\![X]\!]$ of the series $\sum_n \bar a_n X^n$ arising from cusp forms $f$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients `qCoeff f n` are rational integers $a_n$, reduced coefficientwise into $F$; (ii) `IsModPEigen N S k φ lam`, i.e. $\varphi\neq 0$ and for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\notin S$ one has `heckePS k ℓ φ` $=\lambda_\ell\varphi$, where `heckePS` has $n$-th coefficient $a_{n\ell}+\ell^{k-1}a_{n/\ell}$ (the second term present only when $\ell\mid n$); (iii) for every prime $q$ with $q\mid N$ and $q\notin S$ one has [`PowerSeries.heckeU q φ`](def/PowerSeries_FormalHeckeOperators.html#L11) $=\mu_q\varphi$, where [`PowerSeries.heckeU q`](def/PowerSeries_FormalHeckeOperators.html#L11) sends $\sum_n a_nX^n$ to $\sum_n a_{qn}X^n$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from `heckeAlgebra N k S`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_k(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin k` for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin k` for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$, to $F$, such that $\theta(\mathrm{T}_\ell)=\lambda_\ell$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and $\theta(\mathrm{U}_q)=\mu_q$ for every prime $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$, the generators being taken as the elements `heckeAlgebra.T` and `heckeAlgebra.U` of the subalgebra.
--
--   This is one direction of the mod $p$ dictionary between systems of Hecke eigenvalues occurring in the reduction of the integral cuspidal lattice and characters of the Hecke algebra with values in a field of characteristic $p$, in the style of Deligne–Serre. It is used in the construction of characters of the Hecke algebra attached to mod $p$ eigenforms, notably in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_isMaximal_two_ringHom_of_succ_of_map_T_eq_zero_of_five_le_or_exists_prime_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_isMaximal_two_ringHom_of_succ_of_map_T_eq_zero_of_five_le_or_exists_prime_dvd) and in the theta-cycle argument [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.thetaCycle_exists_ringHom_mul_two_apply_eq_of_ringHom_succ_of_eq_three_imp_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.thetaCycle_exists_ringHom_mul_two_apply_eq_of_ringHom_succ_of_eq_three_imp_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
